  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "If $|X|=0$ then $|P(P(P(X)))|=$",
  "worked_solution": "For any set $S$, we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $|X|=0.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n|P(X)|={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(X)))| & ={2}^{|P(X))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(P(X))| & ={2}^{|P(P(X)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
